@flexiarg ways-of-working/backlog-understood
@title Every open item is placed under a way of working, or declared retired
@keywords way of working, invariant, cascade live
@audience agents, operators, institution designers
@tone normative
@style pattern
@status draft 2026-11-02 by claude-16; runs correct it
@provenance declared in futon3c/holes/excursions/ways-of-working.json (claude-2 with Joe, 2026-11-02)
@why [creativity-commons/process-fits-local-conditions stack-coherence/ready-blocked-triage]

! conclusion: The draw pile is empty: every mission, excursion and ticket on the stack has a placement (wing, action, finish) or a retirement, and the placements are on a committed path.

  + IF:
    Thousands of backlogged items that nobody has read are a pile, not a plan; neither the operator nor the War Machine can select from a pile.

  + HOWEVER:
    Items accumulate faster than anyone reads them, and a selector picks from whatever it can see. A status line goes stale in either direction.

  + THEN:
    The draw pile is empty: every mission, excursion and ticket on the stack has a placement (wing, action, finish) or a retirement, and the placements are on a committed path.

  + BECAUSE:
    A pile cannot be selected from. An item is retired when the problem it addresses is solved, not when its mechanism has gone.

  + VALIDATION:
    Is the draw pile empty, with placements on a committed path?
